{"skill":{"slug":"notion-cli","displayName":"Notion Manager"},"version":{"version":"0.0.1","createdAt":1770245226102,"changelog":"Version 1.0.0\n\n- Initial release of notion-cli skill.\n- Provides comprehensive CLI documentation for interacting with Notion pages, databases, and blocks.\n- Includes setup instructions, environment requirements, and authentication setup.\n- Features usage examples for searching, retrieving, creating, updating, and querying Notion content.\n- Details property formats and common command patterns for managing Notion data via the CLI.\n- Lists key capabilities such as interactive mode, multiple output formats, and complex filter support.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":5343,"sha256":"e391575ae5bc22aebf5ab63b9e76aa698875eaa84289cb31ee7c811823616720","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4996,"sha256":"3700c5290d37de58c4c91aea8435267afa3b4b4f10943ec95988943d3adae775","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2129,"sha256":"4c119fffb38fd16431841c93ac9f2d48f72d585f1f4d9a80dd164a5b38a98d05","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033384476,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b380db4b6f32d347b193b2d6a5c67be26f924f7ae3ed3b46bbed10a0ada4d1f2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b380db4b6f32d347b193b2d6a5c67be26f924f7ae3ed3b46bbed10a0ada4d1f2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: notion-cli\nVersion: 0.0.1\n\nThe OpenClaw skill bundle for Notion CLI is classified as benign. All instructions and commands in SKILL.md and README.md are directly related to managing Notion content via the `notion-cli` tool or direct Notion API calls using `curl`. The skill properly handles the `NOTION_TOKEN` for authentication with the legitimate Notion API endpoint (api.notion.com). There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized destinations, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent's behavior beyond its stated purpose. The installation of `@iansinnott/notion-cli` via npm is a standard practice for CLI tools.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161373751},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":44,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":13,"checkedAt":1789033384476},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Notion skill is coherent, but it asks users to install an unpinned global npm package and store a Notion token in plaintext before using commands that can modify live Notion data.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of NOTION_TOKEN and api.notion.com is proportionate for a Notion integration, and access is constrained by pages/databases shared with the integration.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The setup instructs a global unpinned install of @iansinnott/notion-cli, while the referenced homepage points to a different GitHub namespace, so the reviewed skill does not tightly bind users to a reviewed package version or provenance.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Read and write operations are shown with explicit create/update wording, but the examples do not clearly separate read-only use from live mutating POST/PATCH operations or call out confirmation expectations.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill recommends writing the Notion API key to ~/.config/notion/api_key and exporting it without permissions guidance, secret-manager guidance, or warnings about shell history and local exposure.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to create, read, and update Notion pages, databases, and blocks, and the documented Notion API and notion-cli operations match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. Pin and verify the npm package version if possible, consider installing it in an isolated environment instead of globally, use a minimally scoped Notion integration, share only the specific pages or databases needed, and store NOTION_TOKEN in a secure credential store or at least a chmod 600 file rather than a broadly readable plaintext file.","findings":"[T08] unexpected: Installing a CLI is expected for this skill, but a global unpinned third-party npm install with unclear package-to-repository provenance is broader than necessary and remains a material review concern.\n[T09] expected: A Notion token is expected for the stated integration, but the documented plaintext storage lacks restrictive permission or secret-handling guidance.\n[RA2] expected: Credential persistence supports repeated CLI use, but the artifact-backed issue is insecure local secret storage rather than rogue-agent persistence.\n[SQP-2] expected: Create and update examples are purpose-aligned and visibly mutating, but users should treat them as live writes to Notion content.\n[E1] expected: Traffic to https://api.notion.com is the expected Notion API destination and is not evidence of unrelated exfiltration in this artifact.\n[SQP-3] expected: French README text and French sample content are usability/localization notes, not security concerns for this verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033384476}}}}}